$NetBSD$

Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted).
Upstream: Chromium base/logging.cc.
Status: local NetBSD/official fix; not submitted upstream.

OFFICIAL_BUILD defines NDEBUG, so DisplayDebugMessageInDialog (the only reader
of show_error_dialogs) is compiled out. SetShowErrorDialogs still assigns the
variable, which trips -Werror,-Wunused-but-set-global on the target toolchain.
Mark the global [[maybe_unused]].

--- a/base/logging.cc
+++ b/base/logging.cc
@@ -238,7 +238,7 @@ bool g_log_tickcount = false;
 const char* g_log_prefix = nullptr;
 
 // Should we pop up fatal debug messages in a dialog?
-bool show_error_dialogs = false;
+[[maybe_unused]] bool show_error_dialogs = false;
 
 // An assert handler override specified by the client to be called instead of
 // the debug message dialog and process termination. Assert handlers are stored
